0", "kind": "acquisition_assessed", "payload": {"domain": "unassigned_problem", "evidence": "source-36535cab43ba48d9", "outcome": "routing_progress", "persistent_identifiers": ["doi:10.1103/physrevb.101.094510", "doi:10.1103/physrevb.107.115147", "arxiv:2303.17631"], "project": "autonomous-gap-id", "research_id": "immediate-dd24f588ce2e9768", "route": "www.bing.com:discovery", "source_candidate_identities": {}, "source_candidates": ["https://link.aps.org/accepted/10.1103/PhysRevB.101.094510", "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2303.17631", "https://link.aps.org/accepted/10.1103/PhysRevB.107.115147", "https://arxiv.org/html/2412.20743v1", "https://www.nature.com/articles/s42005-022-00819-0.pdf"], "stage": "discovery"}, "prev_hash": "4c27ede1605d738e4db2f0fca7c35394019032c74060af618db58ae1ef657fe1", "hash": "dc60c700b4be43deee62b078464592c02e729fc79b6c556a070cdaf6a5365caf"}, {"seq": 2744, "time": "2026-10-25T11:03:49.146166+00:00", "kind": "observation", "payload": {"actor": "collector", "content": "{\"url\": \"https://www.bing.com/search?q=mechanisms+for+autonomous+research+gap+prioritization+in+open-ended+learning+systems&format=rss\", \"scope\": \"Bing public search snippets and links, including indexed discussions; discovery only, not retrieved articles\", \"excerpt\": \"{\\\"query\\\": \\\"mechanisms for autonomous research gap prioritization in open-ended learning systems\\\", \\\"results\\\": [{\\\"title\\\": \\\"Weyl superconductor phases in a Weyl-semimetal/superconductor ...\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://link.aps.org/accepted/10.1103/PhysRevB.101.094510\\\", \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"This model realizes Weyl-semimetal and Weyl-superconductor phases in the presence of spin-orbit coupling and a chiral-\\\\\\\\(p\\\\\\\\)-wave superconducting order, respectively.\\\"}, {\\\"title\\\": \\\"Higher-order topological superconductors from Weyl semimetals\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://scipost.org/SciPostPhys.12.2.053/pdf\\\", \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"Abstract We propose that doped Weyl semimetals with time-reversal and certain crystalline symmetries are natural candidates to realize higher-order topological superconductors, which exhibit a fully gapped bulk while the surface hosts robust gapless chiral hinge states. We show that in such a doped Weyl semimetal, a featureless finite-range attractive interaction favors a p+ip pairing symmetry ...\\\"}, {\\\"title\\\": \\\"d-wave Charge- Superconductivity From Fluctuating Pair ...\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2303.17631\\\", \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"We present a theory for charge-4e superconductivity as a leading low-temperature instability with a nontrivial d-wave symmetry. We show that in several microscopic models for the pair-density-wave (PDW) state, when the PDW wave vectors connect special parts of the Fermi surface, the predominant interaction is in the bosonic pairing channel mediated by exchanging low-energy fermions. This ...\\\"}, {\\\"title\\\": \\\"Topological order in interacting semimetals\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://link.aps.org/accepted/10.1103/PhysRevB.107.115147\\\", \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"This state is obtained starting from a magnetic Weyl semimetal with a single pair of nodes, separated by half a reciprocal lattice vector. These nodes may be gapped by breaking the \\\\\\\\( U(1) \\\\\\\\) charge conservation symmetry while forming a superconducting state with intra-nodal pairing.\\\"}, {\\\"title\\\": \\\"Magnetic excitations and interactions in the Weyl ferrimagnet ...\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://arxiv.org/html/2412.20743v1\\\", \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"Our work serves as the first comprehensive experimental study of magnetic excitations and interactions in a rare-earth-based Weyl semimetal, setting the stage for study of isostructural Weyl semimetals, and demonstrates the vital role of crystalline symmetry in understanding the role of Weyl fermions on helical magnetic order.\\\"}, {\\\"title\\\": \\\"Second Chern Number Protected Gapless Vortex Modes in ...\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://hub.valency.io/works/W_vhvdphvb_v1\\\", \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"It is found that the vortex line can host gapless chiral Majorana modes in the pair density wave phase of a Weyl semimetal breaking time reversal symmetry [61].\\\"}, {\\\"title\\\": \\\"Spectroscopic signatures of time-reversal symmetry breaking ...\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s42005-022-00819-0.pdf\\\", \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"The collective mode spectrum of a symmetry-breaking state, such as a superconductor, provides crucial insight into the nature of the order parameter. In this work, we study two collective modes ...\\\"}]}\", \"excerpt_truncated\": false, \"source_sha256\": \"81a686cf1ce545934331b917f7d914611bf1c24ce6b6a2f929f0a8600eb60aba\", \"verification_required\": true, \"topic_domain\": \"unassigned_problem\", \"evidence_role\": \"discovery\", \"host_tier\": \"discovery\", \"source_identity\": null, \"persistent_identifiers\": [\"doi:10.1103/physrevb.101.094510\", \"doi:10.1103/physrevb.107.115147\", \"arxiv:2303.17631\"], \"source_candidates\": [\"https://link.aps.org/accepted/10.1103/PhysRevB.101.094510\", \"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2303.17631\", \"https://link.aps.org/accepted/10.1103/PhysRevB.107.115147\", \"https://arxiv.org/html/2412.20743v1\", \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s42005-022-00819-0.pdf\"], \"source_candidate_identities\": {}}", "id": "source-36535cab43ba48d9", "scope": "collected", "source": "https://www.bing.com/search?q=mechanisms+for+autonomous+research+gap+prioritization+in+open-ended+learning+systems&format=rss"}, "prev_hash": "2a28ba7f37cfd25c1bc9df62c2fbf7fa61a66eddda5c3e7eeec750c9d0b86667", "hash": "4c27ede1605d738e4db2f0fca7c35394019032c74060af618db58ae1ef657fe1"}, {"seq": 2743, "time": "2026-10-25T11:01:06.452687+00:00", "kind": "research_planned", "payload": {"id": "w-f9822f13d09943ea", "metadata": {"model_version": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "provider_attempts": [{"elapsed_ms": 1815, "finish_reason": "STOP", "http_status": 2